# Vercel Skills Compliance

This project uses vercel-labs/agent-skills. Follow these rules on every edit:

## Performance (vercel-react-best-practices)

- Use `Promise.all([...])` for independent async calls; never sequential await when parallel is possible
- Use `.toSorted()` or `[...arr].sort()` instead of mutating `.sort()` on state/props
- Prefer `useState(() => expensiveInit())` for lazy state init
- Use functional setState when next state depends on previous: `setCount(c => c + 1)`
- Use SWR for client data fetching (not raw fetch when dedup is needed)

## Composition (vercel-composition-patterns)

- Prefer composition over boolean props (e.g. `isLoading`, `isError`)
- Use compound components and children; avoid render props when composition works
- React 19: use `use()` for context; ref as normal prop instead of forwardRef

## Bundle

- lucide-react and @radix-ui/* are in `optimizePackageImports`; no barrel-import workarounds needed
